#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "General questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why aren't more units from Warhammer / Warhammer Total War in the army lists?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:20
msgid ""
"Warmaster Revolution seeks to preserve the original game designed by Rick "
"Priestly as far as possible.  This means the Warmaster army lists are based "
"around units that were available in 6th edition Warhammer, as these were the "
"options available at the time. The army lists are intended to reflect the "
"playstyle of the army as a whole, rather than representing each individual "
"unit variation. Units represent hundreds of troops from the most common "
"troop types associated with the army. You can use alternative models to "
"represent elite versions of units by granting a magic item to an existing "
"unit type. _For example, give a magic sword to a High Elf Spearmen unit to "
"represent High Elf Swordmasters._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:22
msgid "→ Rulebook: xref:introducing-warmaster.adoc[Introducing Warmaster]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "How are different types of units based?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Infantry is based facing the long edge (40mm) of the stand. All other unit "
"types – Cavalry, Chariots, Monsters, Artillery and Machines – are based "
"facing the short edge (20mm)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:32
msgid ""
"There are some exceptions to this rule which are clearly listed in the unit "
"special rules for their army list. For example, Pikemen are Infantry that "
"face the short edge of their base. Harpies and Daemon Flyers are Monsters "
"that face the long edge of their base."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:34
msgid "→ Rulebook: xref:game-values.adoc#Stands[Game Values – Stands]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "On what base size do I mount Warmaster characters?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:43
msgid ""
"Characters may be mounted on either a standard rectangular base of 40mm × "
"20mm, or a circular base up to 25mm in diameter.  [.edit]#In either case, "
"command range is then measured from the edge of the character base#."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:50
msgid ""
"[.edit]#Alternatively#, you may mount characters on larger base sizes, for "
"example to make a diorama. If you do so, you must measure distances from one "
"specific point on their base which is clear to your opponent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:52
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:characters.adoc#odd-size-character-bases[Generals, Wizards "
"& Heroes – Odd size character bases]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "When do stands count as In the Open?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:58
msgid ""
"All stands are considered to be In the Open, unless they are Defended or "
"Fortified. Only Infantry and Artillery can ever claim Defended or Fortified "
"status, when in suitable terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:60
msgid ""
"This is worked out on a stand-by-stand basis. A unit may have some stands In "
"the Open and some that are Defended, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:62
msgid ""
"Stands of Cavalry, Chariots, Monsters, and Machines, count as being In the "
"Open regardless of the terrain they occupy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:64
msgid ""
"When a unit is In the Open, attacks will hit them on a 4+ and normal charge "
"bonus attacks apply."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:67
msgid ""
"In addition, Infantry which is Charging, Pursuing, Retreating or Advancing "
"can never claim Defended status, regardless of terrain or spell effects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:69
msgid "The only exceptions to this rule are the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:72
msgid "The Empire Steam Tank"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:73
msgid "The Kislev War Wagon in laager formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:75
msgid ""
"These units always count as Defended, even though they are machines, and "
"regardless of terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:77
msgid ""
"This means the enemy will hit them on a 5+ and enemy chargers gain no Charge "
"bonus attacks against them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:78
msgid ""
"Cannon shots *ignore* the target's Defended status, so will hit Defended "
"stands on 4+."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:80
msgid ""
"Undead Ethereal Hosts always hit the target in combat on a 4+, but still get "
"no charge bonus against Defended targets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:81
msgid ""
"Stands in Loose Terrain are In the Open, but attackers gain no charge bonus "
"against them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:85
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:shooting.adoc#defended-or-fortified-targets[Shooting – "
"Defended or fortified targets], xref:combat.adoc#attack-modifiers[Combat – "
"Attack modifiers], xref:combat.adoc#defended-fortified-enemy[Defended & "
"fortified enemy]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Line of sight questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do units require Line of Sight at the beginning of their turn in order to charge?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:94
msgid ""
"No. Units require Line of Sight to charge at the beginning of their move, "
"not that start of the turn. So it is entirely possible for one unit that is "
"blocking Line of Sight to move out of the way, granting Line of Sight to "
"another unit before it moves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:96
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:command.adoc#sequence-of-movement[Command – Sequence of "
"movement] (xref:command.adoc#initiative-charge-1[Figure 1], "
"xref:command.adoc#initiative-charge-2[Figure 2])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can stands draw Line of Sight at 180 degrees from their front corners?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:104
msgid ""
"No. In order to draw Line of Sight, the target must be in front of the line "
"that extends 180 degrees from the front corners of a stand. If in doubt "
"place the straight edge of a suitably sized piece of paper against the front "
"of the unit claiming Line of Sight. The paper represents the Line of Sight "
"zone. If the target unit's base occupies any part of the paper, you can draw "
"Line of Sight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:107
msgid ""
"Units wishing to shoot at chargers that connect with their flank cannot do "
"so unless any stand from the charging unit is forward of the 180 degree line "
"at any point before, during or after the charge move."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:110
msgid ""
"Remember, the Line of Sight is blocked by the presence of other stands, "
"friendly or enemy. This prevents missile units in column drawing line of "
"sight sideways out of the column."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:112
msgid "The only exceptions are units that have 360 degree line of sight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:116
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:game-values.adoc#line-of-sight[Game Values – Line of sight] "
"(xref:game-values.adoc#line-of-sight-target[Figure 3])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "When Shooting, can a unit draw Line of Sight through gaps of less than 1 cm?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:121
msgid ""
"No. To draw Line of Sight when shooting, a unit must have at least 1cm width "
"unobstructed on the edge from which it is rdawing line of sight, *and* be "
"able to extend this unobstructed 1cm width in a straight line to the target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:123
msgid "→ Rulebook: xref:shooting.adoc#targets[Shooting – Targets]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "How do Hills block Line of Sight?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:138
msgid ""
"Hills block Line of Sight beyond their highest elevation point. Line of "
"Sight is blocked by a hill terrain piece that lies completely between two "
"stands which are not on the hill.  Units may draw Line of Sight to other "
"units on a Hill provided the Line of Sight does not go beyond the highest "
"elevation point.  If line of sight is drawn to or from a stand positioned on "
"a hill, only parts of the hill that are higher than both stands block line "
"of sight between them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:141
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:game-values.adoc#the-effect-of-terrain[Game Values – The "
"effect of terrain], xref:movement.adoc#terrain[Movement – Terrain]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:143
#, no-wrap
msgid "Movement questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "When stands in a unit pivot to turn 180 degrees, how much movement does this cost?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:153
msgid ""
"Pivoting a unit’s stands can occur as part of a unit’s directional move, or "
"stands in a unit can make a 180 degree pivot on the spot. To work out how "
"much movement this takes up, follow these rules:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pivot 180 degrees during a move"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:162
msgid ""
"Measure the distance travelled by the corner moving the furthest distance. "
"This will be from the corner of the stand diagonally opposite to the stand’s "
"final position, as shown in diagrams below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:164
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:183
msgid "→ Rulebook: xref:movement.adoc#the-move[Movement – The move]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pivot on the spot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:181
msgid ""
"Stands can pivot on the spot without physically rotating in a circle. "
"Imagine the troops performing an about face manoeuvre on their own base, "
"with the front rank swapping places with the back rank. The movement "
"distance involved is the distance travelled by one corner to the opposite "
"corner, which is 4½cm for a standard Warmaster base. This does not cause the "
"pivoting stand to intersect with other stands in the same unit. Note that "
"this means that Artillery stands are permitted to about face on the spot "
"with a failed order and a half pace move of 5cm. See diagram below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "How does the displacement of a character that is touched by an enemy unit work?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:203
msgid ""
"A character piece that is not already joined to a friendly unit may move to "
"join a friendly unit within 30cm when an enemy unit touches their base. Move "
"the character when the first enemy stand contacts the character base. The "
"character must be able to trace a path to a friendly unit around impassable "
"terrain and enemy units, unless they have a flying mount, in which case they "
"can move over them.  However, the displaced character is permitted to pass "
"through the stands of the enemy unit that touches them. This prevents "
"characters from being unfairly surrounded and killed by mobile enemy units "
"such as flyers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:210
msgid ""
"Once the character has been displaced, the enemy unit may continue its move "
"if possible. Remember that a flying unit that is moved via an order to "
"displace a character has landed, so cannot continue moving without an "
"[.edit]#additional# order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:212
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:characters.adoc#enemy-moving-through-characters[Generals, "
"Wizards & Heroes – Enemy moving through characters]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "How does Maximising Frontage work, including when charging more than one enemy?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:222
msgid ""
"Charging stands must place as much of the front edge of the base as possible "
"in contact with the enemy when they form a battle line. This also extends to "
"any enemy units in line with the original target of the charge.  So if a "
"charging stand can only fit half of its frontage in contact with the "
"original target of the charge, but can fit all of its frontage in contact "
"with a stand from the original target and a stand from another enemy unit in "
"line, it must do this. However if the charging unit can fit all of the "
"frontage of all of its stands against the target unit, without touching any "
"adjacent enemy stands, it will do this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:226
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:movement.adoc#the-charge-move[Movement – The charge move], "
"xref:movement.adoc#forming-a-battle-line[Forming a battle line], "
"xref:movement.adoc#contact-with-other-enemy[Contact with other enemy]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:240
msgid ""
"Each stand must be placed in the battle line in such a way that as much of "
"its front edge as possible makes contact with the enemy. This is called "
"‘maximising frontage’. If it is impossible to place a stand into the battle "
"line so that its front edge makes contact with an enemy, then it must be "
"placed so that its front corner touches an enemy if it can. This means that "
"the maximum number of charging stands will be drawn into the combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:248
msgid ""
"The diagrams below show how a charging unit will maximise frontage against "
"an enemy that has a different base orientation to them. All charging stands "
"can be placed with all of their frontage in contact with the enemy, so they "
"must do this."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:255
msgid ""
"In this Diagram, the charging unit has not maximised frontage. This charge "
"is illegal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:271
msgid ""
"If there are other enemy units adjacent to the target unit then the "
"obligation to ‘maximise frontage’ extends to these other units too. So, "
"where there is another enemy stand aligned to the target unit, a charging "
"stand must be placed against this second enemy if this is its only way to "
"maximise frontage. However, chargers will always maximise frontage against "
"the unit they originally charged where they can do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:279
msgid ""
"The diagrams below show how a charging unit will maximise frontage against "
"two enemy units that have a different base orientation to them. All charging "
"stands can be placed with all of their frontage in contact with the enemy, "
"so they must do this."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:284
msgid ""
"In this diagram, the charging unit has not maximised frontage. This charge "
"is illegal."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:294
msgid ""
"This diagram shows how a charging unit will maximise frontage against the "
"unit it originally charged when able to do so. Although there is a second "
"enemy unit that is closer to the charging stands, all charging stands can be "
"placed with all of their frontage in contact with the original target enemy, "
"so they must do this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can a Flying unit make a Home Back move to disengage from combat?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:302
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:554
msgid "No."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:304
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:313
msgid "→ Rulebook: xref:flying-units.adoc#home-back[Flying Units – Home back]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "Does a flying unit need to be more than 20cm from all friendly characters, or just one, to be able to home back?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:311
msgid ""
"Flyers may only Home Back if they are more than 20cm from *all* friendly "
"characters [.edit]#at the start of# the Command phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:315
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combat questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:318
#, no-wrap
msgid "Does a unit in close combat have to make attacks?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:322
msgid ""
"Yes. A stand in close combat must direct their attacks against a single "
"enemy unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:324
msgid "→ Rulebook: xref:combat.adoc#attacks[Combat – Attacks]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:326
#, no-wrap
msgid "Are missile armed units obliged to shoot if they are able to do so? Do they have to shoot at enemy units that charge them?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:331
msgid ""
"No, a unit doesn't have to shoot. They can hold fire. But if the unit does "
"choose to shoot, all stands must do so if they can."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:334
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:shooting.adoc#targets[Shooting – Targets], "
"xref:shooting.adoc#shooting-at-charging-enemy[Shooting – Shooting at "
"charging enemy]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:336
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can a stand in combat be reduced to 0 Attacks?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:342
msgid ""
"Yes, but remember that if all a unit’s stands in combat have been reduced to "
"0 Attacks then the unit as a whole gets to make 1 Attack as per the Last "
"Ditch Dice rule."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:344
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:366
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:combat.adoc#attack-modifiers[Combat – Attack modifiers]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:346
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a stand can support in combat, must it support?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:350
msgid ""
"Yes. Support is not optional. Any Infantry stand that is in a supporting "
"position will provide support towards the combat result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:353
msgid ""
"Also remember that an infantry stand placed into a supporting position means "
"the entire infantry unit counts as \"in combat\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:355
msgid "→ Rulebook: xref:combat.adoc#support[Combat – Support]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:357
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagram under xref:combat.adoc#pursuit-supporting[Supporting pursuits] shows a victorious unit pursuing a unit that has retreated. The stand on the right of this is now contacting a unit to the front, and along its left edge. Is it being flanked in this example image?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:364
msgid ""
"No. Stands do not apply the enemy in flank or rear penalty to attacks for "
"side to side contact that often occurs in pursuits. The enemy in flank or "
"rear attack penalty only applies to stands that have the front edge of an "
"enemy stand in their flank or rear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:368
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a unit pursues an enemy that has retreated, can it wrap around to surround all edges of the enemy unit, as long as the stands remain touching? Or does it need to maximise contact to the front first?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:371
msgid "Work out each pursuing unit's pursuit on a stand-by-stand basis."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:376
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Basic pursuit* – If a stand can pursue straight forwards so that its front edge contacts a retreating enemy stand,\n"
"it must do this. Once all stands from the unit that can pursue straight forwards have done so, any remaining\n"
"stands in the pursuing unit can be placed into formation as the owning player wishes, including into support, or\n"
"into the flanks or rear of the retreating enemy, provided they do not exceed a full pace move.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:382
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Indirect pursuit* – If there are no enemy stands directly in front of a pursuing unit's stands, and it can draw line\n"
"of sight to the retreating unit, then take any one stand from the pursuing unit that has a clear path to the\n"
"retreating enemy and move it into base contact with the nearest visible retreating enemy stand, exactly as you\n"
"would for a charge. Any remaining pursuing stands can then be placed as you wish in the same way as for basic\n"
"pursuits.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:386
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:combat.adoc#moving-pursuers[Combat – Moving pursuers], "
"xref:combat.adoc#basic-pursuit[Combat – Basic pursuit], "
"xref:combat.adoc#indirect-pursuit[Combat – Indirect pursuit]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:387
#, no-wrap
msgid "Typical combat with pursuits"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:397
msgid ""
"The following diagrams show a typical combat.  Units A and B are infantry in "
"line, with A supporting B.  Units C (infantry) and D (cavalry) are the "
"charging attackers.  (Due to the distance moved, unit C could not achieve "
"maximum frontage against unit B, which allowed Unit D to fit two stands into "
"the combat.)  Units A and B are in combat with units C and D."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:403
msgid ""
"A and B lose the combat.  B removes casualties, and the surviving stands "
"from both units then retreat."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:408
msgid ""
"The stands from units C and D able to pursue straight forward into front "
"edge contact with the enemy must do so:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:418
msgid ""
"Note that one stand from unit C has to contact unit A, and is therefore "
"flank-to-flank with unit B.  In the next diagram, pursuing stands that do "
"not have to pursue straight forwards may now be placed in formation with the "
"rest of their units, as the player wishes, including into the flank or rear "
"where possible.  No pursuing stand may move further than a full-pace move.  "
"This shows one option:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:425
msgid ""
"Note there is no requirement for stands that do not have to pursue straight "
"forwards to be moved into contact with the enemy.  Unit C could move a stand "
"into support, and unit D can form up a line."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:427
msgid "The examples continue with this arrangement."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:432
msgid ""
"After the second round of combat, unit B has been wiped out, and unit A has "
"retreated again.  All units have lost a stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:438
msgid ""
"Unit C pursues straight forwards again, keeping one stand in support.  "
"However unit D no longer has any enemy stands directly in front.  It can "
"still see the retreating enemy, so it can make an Indirect Pursuit."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:445
msgid ""
"An Indirect Pursuit requires the unit to pick one stand and align it to the "
"retreating enemy as if for a charge, so we check to see if the cavalry are "
"now in the front or the flank of unit A.  They are in the flank."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:449
msgid "Unit D moves one stand into contact with the flank of unit A."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:454
msgid ""
"Finally, the remaining stand can be placed as in basic pursuit, for example "
"to the rear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:459
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can a non-flying unit pursue flyers when charging into their flank or rear?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:463
msgid ""
"Yes, non-flying units can pursue flyers when the charging unit charged a "
"flying unit in the flank or rear. It works in the same way as cavalry being "
"charged into flank or rear by infantry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:465
msgid ""
"→ Rulebook: xref:combat.adoc#which-units-can-pursue[Combat – Which units can "
"pursue?]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:467
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unit specific questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:470
#, no-wrap
msgid "When Trolls regenerate, does each stand heal one wound, or does the unit heal a wound?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:477
msgid ""
"The unit recovers one outstanding hit that round, after casualties are "
"removed. Remember hits are recorded against units as a whole, rather than "
"individual stands. For example, a unit of Trolls in combat suffers 5 unsaved "
"hits. This is sufficient to remove one stand of Trolls, and 2 hits are "
"carried over on the unit. At the end of the combat round, 1 outstanding hit "
"is regenerated and removed from the unit. This leaves just 1 hit carried "
"over into the next round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:481
msgid ""
"Armies book: xref:armies:chaos.adoc#special-rules[Chaos – Special rule 2], "
"xref:armies:goblins.adoc#special-rules[Goblins – Special rule 2], "
"xref:armies:orcs.adoc#special-rules[Orcs – Special rule 2]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:483
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can Dogs of War Pikemen be supported by two stands per side, as their long edge base allows two units with conventional basing to be placed in base to base contact?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:487
msgid ""
"Yes, provided the supporting Infantry stands can fit all of the side edge of "
"their base adjacent to the Pikemen stands side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:489
msgid ""
"Armies book: xref:armies:dogs-of-war.adoc#special-rules[Dogs of War – "
"Special rule 1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:491
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a unit has a special rule that states not to roll for being driven back from shooting (e.g. Flagellants), is that unit immune to confusion from shooting, or do you still roll to see if they’re confused?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:496
msgid ""
"The unit special rules for fanatic style units will state that “They can't "
"be driven back by shooting and do not roll for drive backs.” As you don't "
"roll for drive backs you cannot confuse them on a drive back roll of 6. "
"Other sources of confusion affect them as normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:498
msgid ""
"Armies book: xref:armies:empire.adoc#special-rules[Empire – Special rule 2], "
"several others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:500
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the Daemonic Instability table, does a General with a Wizard upgrade count as a wizard?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:502
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:513
msgid "Yes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:504
msgid "Armies book: xref:armies:daemons.adoc#army-rules[Daemons – Army rules]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:506
#, no-wrap
msgid "Does a wizard need line of sight to a target a unit with a spell?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:509
msgid ""
"Refer to the spell description for the spell. It will state whether the "
"caster requires line of sight or not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:511
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some spells such as the Empire _Ball of Flame_ state that the caster draws a line from themselves to work out the spell's effect. Does this have to be a straight line?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:515
msgid ""
"Armies book: xref:armies:empire.adoc#ball-of-flame[Empire – Ball of Flame]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:517
#, no-wrap
msgid "Are there any restrictions on placing Raised Dead units?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:533
msgid ""
"Yes. Raised Dead cannot be placed so that they split one combat engagement "
"into two or more smaller engagements. This can happen when Raised Dead are "
"placed behind supporting enemy Infantry stands, preventing the supporting "
"enemy Infantry from supporting their friends in combat and instead forcing "
"them to turn to fight the Raised Dead – this is not permitted. In addition, "
"Raised Dead must be placed so that all stands fight or support in the "
"targeted combat engagement.  Provided this rule is followed, then new enemy "
"units may be brought into the targeted combat by incidental contact."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:536
msgid ""
"Armies book: xref:armies:tomb-kings.adoc#raise-dead[Tomb Kings – Raise "
"Dead], xref:armies:vampire-counts.adoc#raise-dead[Vampire Counts – Raise "
"Dead]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:538
#, no-wrap
msgid "How does laagering and unlaagering of a War Wagon work?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:547
msgid ""
"At the beginning of the move, if you have your War Wagon in a column "
"formation and you desire to form a laager move any one stand up to 5 cm "
"distance. Then pivot the stand on the spot into desired position and then "
"place the remaining stand into the formation alongside it. There is no "
"distance limit for the second stand. If a War Wagon starts its move in "
"laager formation it can either move up to 5 cm and remain in laager by "
"simply measuring the distance without changing formation, or the Wagon can "
"move up to 20 cm ending its move in column formation. In that case simply "
"measure the part of the stand that moves the most to find out the maximum "
"distance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/questions-and-answers.adoc:549
msgid ""
"Armies book: xref:armies:kislev.adoc#special-rules[Kislev – Special rules 6]."
msgstr ""

